{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"daredevil-marginal-dodo","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nOn the default (materialized) completion path, a completion-verifier PASS records no material\nfingerprint of its own. When it is signed, `verdict_manifest`\n(`src/rebar/_commands/completion_bundle.py` ~line 166-170) falls back to\n`current_material_fingerprint(ticket_id)`, which reads the LIVE ticket at signing time. A run\ntakes 9 to 11 minutes. If the description is edited during the run, the signature binds the\nEDITED material to a verdict that verified the ORIGINAL text.\n\nA close then reuses it: `_reusable_attested_pass` (`src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py`\n~line 154-157) accepts a signed PASS when its signed material equals the ticket's current\nfingerprint, which it now does. So the edited text is certified complete without ever being\nverified. The close path's own signing (`_sign_completion_and_report`,\n`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py` ~line 312) checks only code drift\n(`verified_at_sha` vs a fresh resolve), not ticket-material drift.\n\nOnly the experimental pinned ticket-view mode records the material it read\n(`_attach_completion_read_basis`, `src/rebar/llm/completion.py` ~line 157-175). It is off by\ndefault (`verify.completion_pinned_ticket_view = false`) and the committed `rebar.toml` does not\nenable it, so the MCP server, CLI, and library all take the unprotected path.\n\nUnlike plan review, there is no under-lock re-check: plan review's `generation.sign_manifest`\nre-collects material and raises `PlanReviewGenerationChanged`; completion has no equivalent.\n\n## Evidence (origin/main 82a91a89f1d, in-process, no LLM)\n\nFresh store, ticket with description D1: fingerprint `1a3ac962405bcd5b`. Edit to D2: fingerprint\n`c4d87eb4bcaacafa`. `verdict_manifest` on a default-path PASS (no `completion_read_basis`, no\n`material_fingerprint`) emits `material: c4d87eb4bcaacafa` — D2, not D1.\n\n## Approach to decide in plan review\n\nPin the material the verifier actually reads, at run start, on the materialized path (set\n`result[\"material_fingerprint\"]` from the same snapshot the run reads), and make\n`verdict_manifest` refuse to sign a PASS with no pinned material instead of reading the live\nticket. Existing signed attestations are not rewritten; they remain subject to the existing\nmaterial currency check.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A default-path completion PASS whose ticket is edited between run start and signing signs\n  the run-start material (or refuses to sign), never the post-edit material. Regression test\n  fails on origin/main.\n- [ ] A close after that edit does not reuse the PASS (`_reusable_attested_pass` returns None)\n  and re-runs verification.\n- [ ] No completion manifest is built from a live material read on any signing path.\n\n## Testing\n```\n.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit -k \"completion and material\" -q\n```","id":"0521-7e68-33f8-40c1","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["completion-gate","gate-integrity"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion PASS signs the ticket material current at signing time, not the material the verifier read"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792379167943163001,"uuid":"52f76848-a24a-49ab-b995-cf3af2b439bc"}